          <h2 id="the-idea" data-source-anchor="the-idea">
            Making the configuration rules reusable
          </h2>
        </header>
        <div class="case-pair">
          <div class="case-copy" data-case-reveal>
            <p>
              For a single product, someone could work through the requirements
              and write down the screens it needed. Across dozens of products,
              many of the same questions, conditions and design components
              recur. Maintaining a separate set of selection rules for every
              product would duplicate that logic. A shared change would then
              require finding and revising every copy of the rule.
            </p>
